 "heroVideo": null,
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "figure",
   "html": "<img src=\"@img:images/P1040528_sml.jpg\" alt=\"equinox beach program\" title=\"minelab equinox settings\" width=\"214\" height=\"120\">"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Why do people go with settings from Youtube videos that are not tried and tested?"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Some people just make the videos with no beach detecting knowledge, for likes and views."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Lots of beaches are very differant in the make up of the sand and what lies beneath, some are very clean"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "with no deep iron or other deep trash, some sand is very mineralised and can vary greatly withing a few yards of walking."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "The minelab Equinox standard programs are a great place to start if your just <a href=\"@beginners-guide-to-metal-detecting/\" data-kind=\"internal\">learning to metal detect</a>"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "and noise cancel and senstivity are usually the only settings you need to change, until you are confident in the use of your metal detector."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "With practice and knowledge gained of how the beach you are detecting is made up, then settings can be adjusted."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "To many false signals and digging of junk targets can leave you frustrated where as a quiet running metal detector will help you find more."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Enjoy the Hobby of metal detecting without/"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "What are your thoughts?? feel free to comment"
  }
 ],
